  "notes": "The UK indie-facing wing of the lane, and the entry's harmony is guitar-shaped rather than keyboard-shaped: \"maj7 and m7 shapes with open strings, add9 and 6/9 colours, ii–V turnarounds, and a habit of ending a phrase on the IV rather than the I\". So the two families are the ii–V turnaround and a cycle that lands on IV, the sevenths carry most of the extension weight, and `susSubstitutionProb` covers the open-string add9 shapes. The band is the catalogue's own 79–103 and the keys are the named even major/minor split. Drums are \"light, dry kit with brushes or soft sticks, snare quiet and slightly late, hats in swung 8ths, and heavy use of tambourine/shaker\", which is the 8th hat base at a low fill density, quiet hat velocities, a modest offGrid window and a percussion layer denser than the kit. Melody is \"high-soprano-light, breathy, low-volume, with small intervals and high syllabic density in the verses resolving to long notes in the chorus\" — the highest register in this batch, near-total stepwise motion, density 4–8 and `endVariation` for the resolution. Bass is \"understated, root-and-third with gentle slides\", which is a kick mirror with a real glide probability and a third in every cell shape. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all drum numbers (the research marks the drum detail as inferred), the melody numbers, and the reading of \"ends on the IV\" as a two-chord family. ⚠ The half-time ballad option the entry requires is not encoded; the straight spine is. ⚠ The 116–178 readings are doubled [LOW-CONF].",
